WEBVTT

00:00.350 --> 00:06.930
Across generation, networks and critical energy infrastructure, field work
depends on controlled instructions and the engineering

00:06.930 --> 00:08.164
evidence behind them.

00:08.164 --> 00:16.389
Before a planned task is approved, reviewers need to know which standard
governs, which revision applies and what the inspection

00:16.389 --> 00:17.212
evidence supports.

00:17.212 --> 00:22.147
Cortessa is designed to help authorised teams investigate that bounded
document estate.

00:22.147 --> 00:29.550
It makes source routes and documentary questions visible without becoming an
operational system or taking the approval decision.

00:30.550 --> 00:36.674
A planned-outage or asset-maintenance pack can connect group engineering
standards, site instructions, inspection records, asset

00:36.674 --> 00:39.123
policies, approved deviations and external references.

00:39.123 --> 00:44.430
Those documents may be maintained by different teams and revised on different
schedules.

00:44.430 --> 00:51.778
The review problem is establishing whether the governing source is present and
current, whether terminology and applicability align,

00:51.778 --> 00:58.310
and whether every important statement can be traced back to evidence the
authorised reviewer can inspect.

00:59.310 --> 01:06.662
The credible starting point is one bounded work pack for a single asset class
and site context.

01:06.662 --> 01:13.149
Agree the approved standards, instructions, inspection evidence and revision
history that form the evaluation corpus.

01:13.149 --> 01:19.203
Define the matched tasks, expected source routes, baseline process and
authorised roles before testing.

01:19.203 --> 01:22.231
Use public, synthetic or explicitly cleared material.

01:22.231 --> 01:29.150
Cortessa is evaluated inside that scope; it does not claim continuous
visibility across an operator's estate.

01:30.150 --> 01:35.002
Cortessa runs on a dedicated sovereign workstation inside the agreed boundary.

01:35.002 --> 01:42.060
The approved corpus, ingestion pipeline, local index, on-device model and
source viewer remain on that machine.

01:42.060 --> 01:46.471
Runtime operation does not depend on a public cloud service.

01:46.471 --> 01:50.882
The operator controls the permitted documents, users and security posture.

01:50.882 --> 01:53.970
Retrieval-only operation remains available as the floor.

01:53.970 --> 02:01.910
Cortessa supports document review; it is not connected to supervisory control,
protection, scheduling or any live operational system.

02:02.910 --> 02:05.973
Audit is the centre of the Cortessa workflow.

02:05.973 --> 02:12.099
It works across the selected work pack rather than waiting for one question at
a time.

02:12.099 --> 02:17.841
It can surface stale or superseded references, missing documentary links,
terminology differences and effectivity questions.

02:17.841 --> 02:24.350
Each candidate enters engineering review; it is not automatically evidence of
equipment failure, non-compliance or unsafe operation.

02:25.350 --> 02:29.813
Every audit result leads back to the passages that created it.

02:29.813 --> 02:36.304
Engineering and assurance specialists can open the source, inspect surrounding
wording and check revision and applicability.

02:36.304 --> 02:41.173
If evidence is absent, Cortessa can refuse rather than fill the gap.

02:41.173 --> 02:48.476
Authorised specialists decide whether the issue is genuine, material, already
controlled or outside scope, then record the outcome

02:48.476 --> 02:50.099
through the existing process.

02:50.099 --> 02:53.750
Verified shows provenance; it does not establish asset condition.

02:54.750 --> 03:00.470
Engineering and operational decisions depend on asset context, site rules and
authorised judgement.

03:00.470 --> 03:07.510
The responsible people decide which document governs, whether a discrepancy
matters and whether work may proceed.

03:07.510 --> 03:11.030
Cortessa makes the evidence route and uncertainty visible.

03:11.030 --> 03:19.390
It does not approve a work pack, determine asset health, authorise an outage
or replace engineering, operations, asset-integrity or

03:19.390 --> 03:20.270
safety authority.

03:20.270 --> 03:24.670
Formal decisions remain in the operator's controlled processes and systems.

03:25.670 --> 03:27.833
Reviewers need more than an answer.

03:27.833 --> 03:34.322
They need the source route, document state and the policy governing what the
system is allowed to present.

03:34.322 --> 03:38.648
Identity, document currency, assertion policy and egress posture are visible
governance concerns.

03:38.648 --> 03:45.137
Local activity can be recorded in a ledger to support review of what the
system did and when.

03:45.137 --> 03:48.021
That record may contribute to an evidence package.

03:48.021 --> 03:54.150
It does not make conclusions correct and does not replace the operator's
work-control, asset or approval record.

03:55.150 --> 03:58.882
Compare matched tasks against the existing review baseline.

03:58.882 --> 04:06.812
Measure time to identify and open the governing instruction, reviewer effort,
cited candidate findings, reviewer usefulness and

04:06.812 --> 04:10.544
duplicate rates, appropriate refusals and sampled source-path reproducibility.

04:10.544 --> 04:14.276
Include difficult revisions, excluded evidence and ambiguous terminology.

04:14.276 --> 04:17.075
Record setup, ingestion and corpus-curation effort.

04:17.075 --> 04:27.804
The evaluation should show where Cortessa helps, where it fails and what must
change before any decision to extend the document set or

04:27.804 --> 04:28.270
workflow.

04:29.270 --> 04:31.495
Bring one controlled work pack.

04:31.495 --> 04:35.499
Agree the asset scope, reviewers, baseline and evidence standard.

04:35.499 --> 04:41.283
Test whether Cortessa helps the team locate governing instructions and
adjudicate documentary questions.

04:41.283 --> 04:47.956
Cortessa claims no energy deployment, outage reduction, availability gain,
cost saving, compliance or safety outcome.

04:47.956 --> 04:51.071
Those results must be measured, not assumed.

04:51.071 --> 04:54.630
Start a conversation about a scoped energy evaluation.
